=== PARITY (vs web TeslaAccountSection.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web component owns a status useQuery (useAuthStatus) + four mutations (useAuthURL /
    useRefreshAuth / useSyncVehicles / useDisconnectAuth) + useToast + useConfirm + useTranslation, and a
    `pillDisconnected` flag mirrored from the global `teslasync:tesla-auth-expired/recovered` document
    events. The native surface mirrors ALL of this behind the P1/S8 seams: status snapshots arrive via
    TeslaAccountSource.onUpdate; authorize/refreshToken/syncVehicles/disconnect are async TeslaAccountActions
    methods; the recovery edge fires TeslaAuthRecoveryNotifying. The view performs NO HTTP.
  Logic ports (executed XCTest):
    • TeslaAccountProjection.expiringSoonDays = web `expiringSoon` IIFE: authed && expires_at && 0 < remaining
      <= SEVEN_DAYS_MS → max(1, ceil(remaining/day)); nil otherwise (unauth / no-expiry / expired / beyond).
    • TeslaAccountProjection.connectionState = web `auth?.authenticated && !pillDisconnected` (connected) vs
      `pillDisconnected ? 'Disconnected' : 'Not connected'`; isAuthenticated gates the button set on
      `auth?.authenticated` ALONE (independent of the pill), exactly like the web button branch.
    • TeslaAccountProjection.resolvePhase = web render branches: loading (no cache) → loading; resolved →
      content; failed-no-cache → error(+retry, the QueryError-equivalent the states contract requires);
      cached status persists behind loading/failed (content stays, failure surfaced inline).
    • TeslaAccountToast.project = web toast.success/error per outcome (tokenRefreshed/disconnected success;
      tokenRefreshFailed/syncFailed/disconnectFailed danger + raw err.message detail; connectFailed neutral).
    • Model.apply auth-recovered edge = web `prevAuthRef === false && isAuthed` → notifyTeslaAuthRecovered()
      + clear pill; the `if (!auth) return` guard means a nil→true first snapshot does NOT fire.
  Composition -> web FadeIn + GlassPanel (header IconBox+title+subtitle; inset status row; flex-wrap button
    row; inline sync-success) reproduced natively: TSFadeIn + TSGlassPanel, TSIconBox shield, connected/
    not-connected status rows, ViewThatFits button bar (TSButton primary/secondary/ghost/destructive),
    ConfirmDialog → .confirmationDialog, useToast → self-dismissing TeslaAccountToastView.
  Shared components -> @/components/ui -> TSGlassPanel/TSButton/TSIconBox + typography tokens;
    @/components/motion -> TSFadeIn; @/components/feedback/Toast -> TeslaAccountToastView. Runtime-string
    pills (expiring-soon "Expires in Nd", freshness, banners) use small token-mirroring views per the
    0009/0217 precedent (LocalizedStringKey-only TSBadge can't express runtime interpolation).
    Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> loading(skeleton) · content[connected | not-connected | token-expired] ·
    error(+retry) · stale(chip + one-shot auto-refresh) · offline(cached + chip) · plus the inline status-
    error, the disconnect-confirm dialog, the four toasts, and the inline sync-count. "empty" maps to the
    friendly not-connected CTA (this surface has no list — it always shows connected/not-connected, never a
    blank box). Each has a #if DEBUG preview and is unit-tested via the projection / model.
    NOTE: the web silently no-ops a failed `auth_url` fetch; the native connect adds a neutral
    `tesla.connectFailed` toast (additive Apple-HIG correctness, not drift) so a launch failure is visible.
  i18n -> all 22 web t() keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web English fallback (tesla.title/
    subtitle/connected/expiringSoon/tokenExpires/disconnected/notConnected/reauth.body/connect/refreshToken/
    syncVehicles/reauthorize/disconnect/synced/disconnectTitle/disconnectConfirm + common.cancel + toast.
    tokenRefreshed/tokenRefreshFailed/syncFailed/disconnected/disconnectFailed), + 11 native chrome keys
    (tesla.connectFailed/offlineDetail/loading/errors.load/retry/live/stale/offline/staleBanner/
